      "writtenOn": "2026-10-02T09:46:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed.\n\nMapping commit-object facts onto a RefPermission inside CommitValidators is the wrong place for a permission decision, and both of these changes kept adding to that layer instead of fixing it.\n\nI am abandoning this change and replacing them with a short series that does it properly, following the existing pattern: Gerrit already keeps object-dependent permission decisions in dedicated server/project/ controls that combine the Git object with a PermissionBackend.ForRef (CreateRefControl, DeleteVoteControl, RemoveReviewerControl).\n\nThe new series, on top of master (change 636985):\n\n1. Move forged-identity checks into ReceiveCommitControl.\n2. Move the merge-commit check the same way; after this no commit-object permission decision remains in the validators.\n3. Allow direct merge pushes on the clean design: the feature from change 258271, with the destination-vs-refs/for scoping in canUploadMerge instead of the validator factory.\n4. Deprecate the legacy refs/for fallback for direct merge pushes (warn + docs only).",
